# Component rules

## Folder placement

- `primitives/` — Radix wrappers, Tailwind-styled. The only place that imports `@radix-ui/*`.
- `atoms/` — single-purpose UI (Badge, Spinner, Input, ThemeToggle…).
- `molecules/` — 2–4 atoms grouped (SearchBar, AvatarName, IconLabel…).
- `organisms/` — self-contained sections (NavHeader, ChatInputDock, MessageBubble…).
- `templates/` — page-level layout skeletons with slots.

## Authoring rules

- Always export named, never default — except for Storybook `*.stories.tsx`.
- Use `React.forwardRef` for any component that wraps an interactive native element.
- Compose class names with `cn(...)`. Pass `className` through last so callers can override.
- Provide stable, descriptive `displayName` on `forwardRef` components.

## Concrete pattern

```tsx
export const Foo = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, FooProps>(
  ({ variant = "primary", className, ...rest }, ref) => (
    <button ref={ref} className={cn(base, variants[variant], className)} {...rest} />
  ),
);
Foo.displayName = "Foo";
```

## Storybook

- Each component must ship a colocated `Component.stories.tsx`.
- Stories cover at minimum: default, variants, disabled (if interactive).
